      "id": 18829,
      "name": "epicraiz",
      "username": "epicraiz",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/epicraiz/{size}/2000_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-12-27T18:23:34.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p><span><span>I will be running the Starter Kit in a few weeks for my group when our DnD campaign comes to an end.</span></span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span><span>One of the players in the group likes to metagame and I’m positive he will read the books in advance (I can provide examples if requested). Has anybody altered the storyline and/or combat encounters to keep the story/game surprising? Looking for outside ideas to help me differentiate my thought process.</span></span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span><span>I’d prefer not to kick him out to preserve friendships. Last time I talked to somebody in the group about cheating (privately of course) ended in the two of us not talking for 6 months and he dropped group.</span></span></p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:19.106Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
