    {
      "id": 224808,
      "name": "jlabrecque42",
      "username": "jlabrecque42",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/ecccb3/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2019-01-02T16:29:37.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I use the books as a framework, but ultimately, anything can change.&nbsp; For instance, in the Void, I seperated the whole party and they were each tested for their worthiness to reach the void crystal.&nbsp; Legacy had to save he daughter (pre powers)&nbsp;from Baron Blade. Wraith had to learn the lesson of relying on her friends.&nbsp;I re-enacted Spite in the bell tower, except she was able to save Sara and Eduardo with the help of the Freedom Five.&nbsp; Absolute Zero had to face a fire breathing dragon in a lava pit to save Tachyon. Tachyon had to outrun Friction and save her from herself. Unity, was faced with a choice between machines and humanity as her best friend, Omnitron X, went rogue and was trying to kill the Freedom Five.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Anyway, the books are just a guide.&nbsp; Espicially issues like Tomb of the Bizzare.&nbsp; Just some room descriptions, a scene tracker, and some ideas for obstacles.&nbsp; It's all up to the GM to create the connective tissue, or just start from scratch and make it your own.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Hope that helps! :)</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:58:17.001Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 1,
