      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I use the books as a framework, but ultimately, anything can change.&nbsp; For instance, in the Void, I seperated the whole party and they were each tested for their worthiness to reach the void crystal.&nbsp; Legacy had to save he daughter (pre powers)&nbsp;from Baron Blade. Wraith had to learn the lesson of relying on her friends.&nbsp;I re-enacted Spite in the bell tower, except she was able to save Sara and Eduardo with the help of the Freedom Five.&nbsp; Absolute Zero had to face a fire breathing dragon in a lava pit to save Tachyon. Tachyon had to outrun Friction and save her from herself. Unity, was faced with a choice between machines and humanity as her best friend, Omnitron X, went rogue and was trying to kill the Freedom Five.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anyway, the books are just a guide.&nbsp; Espicially issues like Tomb of the Bizzare.&nbsp; Just some room descriptions, a scene tracker, and some ideas for obstacles.&nbsp; It's all up to the GM to create the connective tissue, or just start from scratch and make it your own.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hope that helps! :)</p>",
